// A standard output nobody reads ends a printing program (design/v5/spec/10 Review 2026-10-08,
// Go's way): the print whose flush finds the pipe gone ends it quietly of SIGPIPE — what it
// prints after never comes. Run as `program | true`: a megabyte is more than any pipe holds, so
// a flush fails whether or not `true` has gone yet. Expected: no stderr, killed by SIGPIPE.
import std.io { eprintln, println };

fn main(): void {
    for (i in 0..100000) {
        println(f"line {i}");
    }
    eprintln("still here");
}
